†One-stop CDMO Services】\nL4875: \nL4876:   * 【60†Quality Management System】\nL4877: \nL4878:   * 【61†Calculator Application】\nL4879:     * 【592†Molarity Calculator】\nL4880:     * 【593†Dilution Calculator】\nL4881:     * 【594†Density Calculator】\nL4882:     * 【595†Reconstitution Calculator】\nL4883:     * 【596†Specific Activity Calculator】\nL4884:     * 【597†Protein Sequence Alignment Tool】\nL4885:     * 【598†Protein pI, MW and Extinction Coefficient Calculator】\nL4886:     * 【599†DNA Sequence Alignment Tool】\nL4887:     * 【600†DNA/RNA Sequence Conversion Tool】\nL4888:     * 【601†DNA Molecular Weight Calculator】\nL4889: \nL4890: [Input]\nL4891: \nL4892: Cat. No.: HY-119787\nL4893: \nL4894: Copy Link\nL4895: # α-Rubromycin\nL4896: \nL4897: (Synonyms: Collinomycin)\nL4898: α-Rubromycin (Collinomycin) is an 【602†antibiotic】 isolated from the mycelia of Streptomyces collinus. α-Rubromycin also acts as a 【2646†DNA polymerase】 inhibitor, with an IC_{50} of 0.91 μM against bovine mammalian 【2646†DNA polymerase】. α-Rubromycin binds to the active region of 【2646†DNA polymerase】 β, competes with nucleotide substrates for binding, and interferes with template-DNA interactions.\nL4899: α-Rubromycin inhibits the activities of 【731†telomerase】, retroviral 【629†reverse transcriptase】 and terminal deoxynucleotidyl transferase, as well as the growth of Staphylococcus aureus. α-Rubromycin can be used in studies related to 【604†bacterial】 infections.\nL4900: For research use only. We do not sell to patients.\nL4901: \nL4902:   * CAS No.: 【3196†27267-69-2】\nL4903:   * Formula: C_{27}H_{20}O_{12}\nL4904:   * Molecular Weight:536.44\nL4905: \nL4906:   * Storage:\nL4907: \nL4908: Please store the product under the recommended conditions in the Certificate of Analysis.\nL4909: \nL4910:   * 【3197†Data Sheet (281 KB)†file.medchemexpress.com】\nL4911: \nL4912:   * 【3198†Image: Click to View α-Rubromycin Chemical Structure†file.medchemexpress.com】\nL4913: \nL4914: α-Rubromycin Chemical Structure\